        <!-- Closing -->
        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            A <strong class="text-white">Generac generator costs</strong> far more than its sticker price, and pretending otherwise is how homeowners end up with a signed contract and a $3,000 change order. Budget $6,500-9,500 installed for a 10-14kW unit covering essentials, $9,000-13,000 for an 18-22kW unit covering a typical whole home, and $16,000+ once you move into the liquid-cooled Protector line.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            The two moves that save the most money are unglamorous: <strong class="text-white">get three itemized quotes</strong>, and <strong class="text-white">confirm your gas supply can feed the unit</strong> before you sign. Those two steps routinely account for a $3,000-4,000 swing on identical installations.
          </p>
